{
  "analysis": "I'm starting fresh in the /app directory. I need to read the statute file to understand the tax rules, then apply them to Alice's case facts to calculate her 2010 tax liability.",
  "plan": "First, I'll read the statute file to understand the tax rules. Then I'll analyze the case facts and apply the relevant provisions to calculate Alice's tax.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /app/statute.txt\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I've read the statute. It contains tax brackets for different filing statuses (§1), personal exemptions (§151), standard deduction (§152), and marital status rules (§7703). I need to determine Alice's filing status, calculate her taxable income, and compute her tax liability.",
  "plan": "I'll analyze the case facts: Alice is unmarried (no mention of marriage), has gross income of $210,204, paid $45,252 to Bob for work (deductible business expense), paid retirement fund for Bob and health insurance for Charlie (Charlie is retired father, likely a dependent). I need to find the standard deduction amount for unmarried individuals and exemption amounts, then calculate tax.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n 'Unmarried individuals' /app/statute.txt | head -5\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n 'standard deduction' /app/statute.txt | head -10\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n 'exemption amount' /app/statute.txt | head -10\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I found key sections. Section 1(c) covers unmarried individuals with tax brackets. Section 151 has exemption rules with $2,000 exemption amount (line 72). I need to find the basic standard deduction amounts for unmarried individuals and understand what deductions Alice can claim.",
  "plan": "I need to see the basic standard deduction amounts for unmarried individuals. Let me look at lines around 386-396 where the basic standard deduction is defined, and also check the dependency rules for Charlie.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '384,410p' /app/statute.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '36,60p' /app/statute.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n 'dependent' /app/statute.txt | head -20\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I've found the key tax provisions. For unmarried individuals (§1(c)), the tax brackets are: 15% up to $22,100, 28% up to $53,500, 31% up to $115,000, 36% up to $250,000, and 39.6% above $250,000. The standard deduction for 'any other case' (unmarried) is $3,000 (§152(c)(2)(C)). The exemption amount is $2,000 (§151(d)(1)). I need to determine Alice's filing status, calculate her taxable income, and check if Charlie qualifies as a dependent.",
  "plan": "I need to read more of the statute to verify the dependency rules (§152) and confirm the standard deduction amounts. Then I'll calculate Alice's tax by: 1) Determining her filing status (unmarried), 2) Calculating AGI (gross income minus business expenses), 3) Subtracting standard deduction and personal exemptions, 4) Applying the tax brackets.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '99,130p' /app/statute.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '384,400p' /app/statute.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I've gathered key information: Alice is unmarried, has gross income of $210,204. The standard deduction for unmarried is $3,000 (§152(c)(2)(C)). Exemption amount is $2,000 (§151(d)(1)). Tax brackets for unmarried are in §1(c). I need to determine what deductions Alice can claim and if Charlie qualifies as a dependent.",
  "plan": "I need to check the dependency rules (§152) for qualifying relative status, and look at what business expenses Alice can deduct. Then calculate her taxable income and tax.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '130,180p' /app/statute.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '250,300p' /app/statute.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I found dependency rules. Charlie (Alice's father) would qualify as a 'qualifying relative' under §152(d)(2)(C) - he's the father. He retired in 2009 so likely has no income in 2010. I need to find the section on deductions from gross income to calculate Alice's AGI, and also check if the retirement fund and health insurance payments are deductible.",
  "plan": "I need to find the section that defines what deductions are allowed from gross income to get AGI. Then calculate taxable income and tax.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n 'deduction for AGI\\|adjusted gross income' /app/statute.txt | head -20\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '200,250p' /app/statute.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I found that §152(b)(1) defines head of household status. Charlie could make Alice a head of household since he's her father and retired (no income). I need to find the section that lists deductions from gross income to calculate AGI, and then compute the tax.",
  "plan": "I need to find the section defining deductions from gross income (often §62 or similar). Then I'll calculate Alice's AGI, taxable income, and tax liability.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n '^§62\\|^§162\\|^§212\\|^§213\\|^§401' /app/statute.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '180,220p' /app/statute.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I need to find the section defining deductions from gross income (AGI). Let me search for sections that list deductible expenses.",
  "plan": "Search for sections that define deductions from gross income, particularly looking for business expenses, retirement contributions, and health insurance deductions.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n 'deductions' /app/statute.txt | head -30\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '220,280p' /app/statute.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I found §366 which defines taxable income for non-itemizers as adjusted gross income minus standard deduction and exemptions. I need to find the section defining what deductions are allowed in arriving at AGI (often business expenses, retirement contributions, etc.).",
  "plan": "Search for sections that define deductions from gross income, particularly looking for business expenses (§162), self-employed retirement, and health insurance deductions.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n '^§[0-9]\\+\\.' /app/statute.txt | head -30\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '330,380p' /app/statute.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I found §63 which defines taxable income. For non-itemizers, taxable income = AGI - standard deduction - personal exemptions. I need to find §62 which defines adjusted gross income and what deductions are allowed to arrive at AGI.",
  "plan": "Search for §62 to find what deductions are allowed from gross income to calculate AGI, particularly looking for business expenses and retirement/health insurance deductions.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '320,360p' /app/statute.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n '§62' /app/statute.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The statute doesn't appear to have §62. I need to find what deductions are allowed to arrive at AGI. Let me search for sections about business expenses, retirement contributions, or health insurance.",
  "plan": "Search for sections that might define what deductions reduce gross income to AGI, particularly looking for business expenses (§162), retirement, and health insurance.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "grep -n 'business\\|retirement\\|health' /app/statute.txt | head -30\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '280,330p' /app/statute.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ]
}

